\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Ringgit recoups against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1997\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 15 (Reuter) - A stronger U.S. dollar in Asia kept most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin defensive trade on Tuesday, but with some rises capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ringgit drifted past significant support at 2.51 against the dollar early, spurred by investment bank demand. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's rise was capped later by selling of dollar/ringgit on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara. \par \par \uc2  "Investment banks were buying sizeable amounts until Bank Negara started checking," a Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer with a local bank confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's checking, which restrained the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/ringgit was at 2.5090/2.5095 at 0430 GMT against 2.5070/2.5080 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was also slightly weaker against the dollar due to sufficient liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Corporates due for weekly tax settlements on Tuesday and the hike in statutory reserve requirements appeared able to meet demand, which was helped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injection of 847 billion rupiah on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The new reserve rate of five percent, which takes effect on Wednesday, was expected to drain five to eight trillion rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity, however, should keep rupiah well supported at 2,409 against its U.S. counterpart, although dollar strength overseas may inhibit the rate's upside, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/rupiah was at 2,405.60/2,406.00 compared with 2,404.50/2,404.75 in late Monday action. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, dollar/Sing activity was subdued with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing its longer-term descent against the greenback on anticipation of higher U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Some ringgit/Sing buying in the morning also worked against the Sing," the dealer with the European broking house said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/Sing eased to 1.4415/1.4425 at mid-session, down from 1.4380/90 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked set to fluctuate within a 1.4300 to 1.4500 band, tending toward its recent low of 1.4520 on the dollar's bullish fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Little interest was sighted for the Thai baht, dampened by the four-day Thai New Year holiday which began on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said outrights had eased marginally to 26.090/26.095 compared with 26.070/26.075 on Monday, and forwards were also holding a bearish tone with buyers sidelined. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand last fixed the daily baht/dollar mid-rate at 26.07 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), James Mclean in Bangkok (662-652-0642) and Jacqueline Wong in Singapore (65-8703088) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4f072ty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
