\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Down Vs U.S. Dollar On Various Factors \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 05:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was down against the U.S. dollar in early trading Thursday, as the dollar continued to be strong against the majors, and players showed little interest in the ringgit, after the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said some players were 'still nervous' about getting involved in the market, after the rumor that Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had made a surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market early Wednesday, to try and stop the ringgit's recent depreciation against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara doesn't comment on rumors of such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers also said that Wednesday's rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keeping players out of the market. But they added that the main reason for the ringgit's depreciation so far Thursday, is that the dollar is continuing to be strong against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the yen and Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  'So far, the main news is still the dollar's strength, against all the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' another locally-based ringgit dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0323 GMT (11:23 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the dollar was at 2.5063 ringgit, up from 2.5047 ringgit late Wednesday, and 2.5060 ringgit early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5049 ringgit and 2.5075 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0334GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02ir3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
