\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Bk Negara Seen Signaling Support For Strong Ringgit \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Hansford \par \uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 14:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday to stem the ringgit's recent depreciation against the dollar, dealers said, signaling its preference for a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While Bank Negara didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, most ringgit dealers said they were quite certain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was responsible for selling some $150 million to buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading. \par \par \uc2  'Players smelled Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market,' said a senior dealer at a well-placed Malaysian bank, who declined to be identified because of the sensitivity of the subject. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit rose strongly as a result, with the dollar trading late Wednesday at 2.5035 ringgit, down from 2.5075 ringgit late Tuesday and well below a peak early Wednesday at 2.5111 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  One locally-based ringgit dealer, who also declined to be named, said Bank Negara had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars around 2.5110 ringgit, pushing the dollar down from its intraday peak. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts agreed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  favors a strong ringgit, both to keep the cost of imports down and to stifle inflationary pressures in the fast-growing Malaysian economy. But it doesn't routinely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and doesn't comment on rumors of such movements. \par \par \uc2  The locally-based dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the ringgit to get any weaker than it did early Wednesday. 'The costs of imports last year was particularly high,' the dealer said. They amounted to 184.0 billion ringgit versus exports of 192.6 billion ringgit. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1213GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902iiz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
