\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Stronger After Rumored  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Move \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 05:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was higher against the U.S. dollar in early Wednesday trading after several days of losses, and dealers said there were rumors that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from depreciating further. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday, and it doesn't comment on market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but several dealers said between $100 million and $200 million had been sold to buy ringgit in early trading, and they said this could have been done by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers point out that the ringgit has weakened against the dollar since the end of last week, and they note that Bank Negara, like other central banks, keeps a close watch on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and often tries to head off both large gains or large losses. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the main reason the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently strengthened against the ringgit is the dollar's gains against the majors. \par \par \uc2  They say another factor contributing to the ringgit's losses is the selling of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Singapore dollars in a bid to cash in on the ringgit's recent gains against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0339 GMT (11:39 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5060 ringgit, down from 2.5075 ringgit late Tuesday, but still slightly up from 2.5050 ringgit early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5045 ringgit and 2.5111 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0359GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902foj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
