\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  acts to stem ringgit fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, April 9 (Reuter) - Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the ringgit's fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in to sell $100-200 million at 2.5120 a dollar. Its selling lasted until ringgit came down to 2.5100, with a bulk of the sales around 2.5110, they said. \par \par \uc2  There was no confirmation from Bank Negara, which does not usually comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was acting through some large Malaysian banks. The intention seems to just slow down the ringgit's fall, not stop it," said a dealer with a large Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  Immediately after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit recovered 50 points to around 2.5060/70 a dollar. At 0300 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.5080/90. \par \par \uc2  Support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also brought in Malaysian exporters, who had been waiting for dollar/ringgit's rise to sell their dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators who had been buying dollar/ringgit this morning also started squaring up as soon as they heard selling from Kuala Lumpur side," said a dealer with another Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  "This exaggerated the volumes after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  However, the strength of dollar/majors would not allow a major correction in dollar/ringgit, which has risen nearly 200 points in the last two days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the morning, dollar/ringgit broke through 2.51/dollar, triggering stop-loss selling, due to which ringgit was expected to decline further. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. hedge fund, squaring up a large three-month position in the ringgit, was said to be responsible for the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy (603-230 7509) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4907kce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
