\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit falls to 2.5098 a dollar as US funds sell. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, April 8 (Reuter) - The ringgit skidded against the U.S. dollar on selling led by U.S. funds and on the back of the surge of the dollar/yen rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0755 GMT, ringgit was quoted at 2.5083/93 a dollar, after falling as low as 2.5098 earlier. It closed in Kuala Lumpur trading on Monday at 2.4965/75. \par \par \uc2  The rise of the Singapore dollar against the ringgit also depressed the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Research house I.D.E.A. said a U.S. hedge fund was believed to be behind the selling via a few investment houses, with an amount believed to total $200 million. \par \par \uc2  "Sources also told us that the recent ringgit selling was related to a large U.S. hedge fund liquidating their long three-month outright position (established in January 1997) which will mature over the coming week," it said. \par \par \uc2  Added a dealer at a large Malaysian bank: "(The U.S. funds) say the best situation now is to pull out especially as the U.S. is more promising -- interest rates are higher and likely to increase." \par \par \uc2  At 2.5098, the ringgit is at its lowest level in three months, since falling to 2.4970 on January 6. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far to support the ringgit. Dealers speculated that Bank Negara would probably only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the ringgit edges lower to 2.51. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basket of trade \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the strength of the dollar is balanced by the weakness of the yen and should therefore be quite neutral on its export-competitiveness, one market analyst said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was propelled to a fresh four-year high against the yen in Tokyo, at 126.12. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the ringgit was also at 1.7413/32 per Singapore dollar, down from 1.7254/73 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4807ifg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
