\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Up Vs U.S. Dollar; 2.4700 Level Watched \b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 03:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was higher against the U.S. dollar in early trading Wednesday as investors in the region snapped up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the basis of the country's sound economy and high interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 0247 GMT (09:47 p.m. EST), the dollar was at 2.4718 ringgit, down from 2.4757 ringgit late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.4710 ringgit and 2.4733 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  A ringgit dealer in Singapore, who declined to be named, said the interest in the ringgit might continue to push the dollar lower but some suspect Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the ringgit from getting too strong against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'Everybody is looking at the 2.4700 ringgit figure to see if Negara is there,' the dealer said. 'If not, they're going to wack it to 2.4500 ringgit.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-03-97 \par \par \uc2  0257GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3c01r6r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
