\par\par \b \uc2  Futures indicate Malaysia interest rates to fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Madhav Reddy \par \uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1996\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 14 (Reuter) - Malaysian interest rates, pushed up by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past year to check inflation, are expected to start softening by mid-1997, futures dealers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They said a declining trend in yields on the interest rate futures market on the Malaysia Monetary Exchange (MME) was setting the direction. \par \par \uc2  "The perception is that interest rates are going to go lower. People have begun buying futures in anticipation of lower interest rates," said K. Sree Kumar, executive director at futures brokerage KAF-Refco Futures Sdn Bhd. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rate futures have begun leading the way for the cash market. And rates look easy on the long end of futures," said the head of money dealing at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the interest rate futures market based on the benchmark three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) had aggressively picked up volumes after languishing for the first two months after its launch at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volumes had been averaging between 350 and 400 lots a day with a growing number of participants, mainly individual members and foreign banks. \par \par \uc2  The MME, Malaysia's second futures bourse, was launched on May 28 to trade in interest rates, bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures. The first market, the Kuala Lumpur Options and Financial Futures Exchange (KLOFFE), trades in stock index futures. \par \par \uc2  A futures dealer with another bank said growing liquidity in the Malaysian money market and apparent inaction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggering speculation that interest rates would come down in the not so distant future. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term interest rates have fallen by nearly 30 basis points in the last few weeks and Bank Negara has not done anything," the dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local interbank money market to check liquidity or set interest rates as part of its inflation-fighting efforts. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara has not been in the market the last two months despite large maturities of government paper and overseas fund inflows that have increased liquidity and pushed rates downward. \par \par \uc2  On the MME, the three-month KLIBOR contract for June 1997 indicated a yield of 7.19 percent at the end of Wednesday's morning session against 7.32 percent in the cash market. \par \par \uc2  The December 1996 contract was at a yield of 7.23 percent and March 1996 at 7.19. \par \par \uc2  Other futures dealers said the trend in the futures market was speculative. The rising inflation and growing current account deficit that forced Bank Negara to tighten its monetary policy earlier this year have not eased. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of the current push I would term as speculative because they are based on a belief that rates would come off, but that may not be the case at all," said Radhakrishnan Nair, executive director at Amanah Futures & Options Sdn Bhd. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the tightening phase is over yet," he said, adding rates may have peaked but may not decline for a while. \par \par \uc2  Sree Kumar of KAF-Refco said that even if rates had peaked, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not allow a sharp decline. "I think many people in the futures market may be caught on the wrong side." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8e049ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
