\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Ringgit retreats on profit-taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 18 (Reuter) - Ringgit trade again dominated exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian unit corrected against the Singapore dollar and the U.S. unit in early Asian trade, sliding back to 2.5000 per U.S. dollar on heavy profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  But dealers are wary of calling for further easing of the ringgit, saying sustained ringgit demand will keep it from falling too sharply. \par \par \uc2  "The 0.5650 is definitely a sell level for the ringgit against the Sing but I would be very wary of shorting the ringgit at these levels right now," said one regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore. "The trend is still for the ringgit-Sing to go up," he added. \par \par \uc2  At about 0430 GMT, the ringgit was trading at 2.4985/95 to the dollar and 0.5628/38 to the Singapore dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets awaited clues for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action as Bank Negara has been notably restrained in its efforts to cap the Malaysian unit's surge over late last week and this week. \par \par \uc2  They said dollar-buying by agents of Bank Negara was also continuing, albeit in small quantities. \par \par \uc2  "But the indication is that it does not want to stop the ringgit's rise. They want this international show of confidence to continue for a while," a Singapore-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Pressure is building up on Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step up its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies in the coming weeks since it faces a series of maturing bills and loans and as foreign funds continue to flood into the country from Japan and from U.S. names unwinding short ringgit positions," said a Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers added, though, that apart from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, ringgit direction may also be affected by the strength of the yen. \par \par \uc2  They said rumours circulating in Japan's money markets that Bank of Japan may tighten monetary policy may boost the yen and add further strength to the Malaysian unit. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, moves by the Bank of Thailand to curb domestic money supply and the inflow of short-term funds on Wednesday left the baht little affected on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The market hasn't reacted a whole lot to the news, it doesn't seem overly concerned," said one strategist for a Singapore bank. "The baht is still trading within a band and the forwards are a bit softer," he added. \par \par \uc2  The baht firmed to 25.305-25.309 to the dollar in early quiet trade from 25.315-25.318 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah firmed against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer in Jakarta said sentiment on the rupiah remained upbeat, possibly on the back of moderately tight liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said uncertainty on the liquidity front appeared to have caused the rupiah to inch closer to the upside of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band. \par \par \uc2  Rupiah was at 2,326.00/7.00 at 0500 GMT against an opening at 2,326.50/27.50. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 0.75/0.85 and tom/next at 2.1/2.2. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy in Kuala Lumpur (603-230-8911), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221-384-6364), Tang Nguyen in Bangkok (662-252-9950) and Valerie Lee in Singapore (65-8703080) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4i094ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
