\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Up Vs U.S. Dlr; Broke Two Support Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 09:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit strengthened against the U.S. dollar Friday, breaking two key support levels, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, they said, began to strengthen overnight when Japanese traders started buying the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Around 0818 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5340 ringgit, down from 2.5427 ringgit late Wednesday, trading between 2.5318 and 2.5380 ringgit during the day. \par \par \uc2  'This is the last week for the Japanese fiscal year, they may have changed their rating to overweight for the ringgit,' an analyst with a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar broke 2.5420 ringgit overnight and 2.5360 ringgit in the morning, he said. \par \par \uc2  'Now we are expecting the dollar to test the 2.5300 ringgit level', he said. \par \par \uc2  The demand for the ringgit was also bolstered by the high Malaysian interest rates, which at around 7.00% make ringgit the favoured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be in, a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to borrow three-month ringgit funds at 7.00%. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were unchanged at 7.08%, while the three-month KLIBOR were slightly down to 7.12% compared with 7.12% Thursday. The six-month remained unchanged at 7.15%. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, was at 6.5% lower than 7.90% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-03-96 \par \par \uc2  0848GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3t02sbt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
