\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Down Vs U.S. Dlr; Thin Volume \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1996\par 09:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was weaker than the U.S. dollar, in thin volume trading Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Though the trading remained subdued, traders said there were a lot of bidders for the dollar in the morning especially from Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5490 ringgit, up from 2.5430 ringgit late Thursday, trading between 2.5430 and 2.5518 ringgit during the day. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a local bank said that earlier in the trading day there was some selling pressure on the ringgit following a report in the Asian Wall Street Journal on the deepening financial crisis at state-owned steelmaker Perwaja Terengganu Sdn. Bhd. \par \par \uc2  The report said the company is unable to pay its 5.7 billion ringgit debt. \par \par \uc2  But dollar/ringgit trading quickly settled into familiar ranges, and stayed lackluster, throughout the trading day, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dr. Daniel Lian, an economist with Natwest Markets Singapore said the selling was minimal, and that the thin volume exaggerated the movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the market is reflecting traders squaring positions ahead of the long holidays, rather than anything else. \par \par \uc2  The market will be closed next week for the dual celebration of Chinese New Year and Muslim Eid Al-Fitr. \par \par \uc2  'Many traders were caught short on the dollar, thus they liquidated their ringgit positions,' said a chief dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  They don't want to be long on the ringgit going into the holidays, he said. \par \par \uc2  Market observers said though there was a spate of figures released this week, like the money supply figures, inflation and production index, it failed to have any significant impact on the dollar/ringgit trading. \par \par \uc2  'As none of the figures was adversely bad, it didn't influence the trading,' he said. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market by borrowing three months ringgit funds at 7.00%, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) was at 7.11%, down from 7.12% Thursday. The three-month KLIBOR was also slightly lower at 7.20%, compared with 7.21% Thursday. The six-month KLIBOR was down to 7.27% from 7.28% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, closed unchanged at 6.50%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0852GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2g01f3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
