\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Slightly Up Vs U.S. Dlr;Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 1996\par 10:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was up against the U.S. dollar, in quiet trading Thursday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  ''Despite the volatility in the dollar against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar hardly moved against the ringgit,'' said a dealer with a local bank. chief dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Trading, dealers said was limited to traders squaring off positions. \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5430 ringgit, down from 2.5440 ringgit late Wednesday, trading between 2.5420 and 2.5445 ringgit during the day. \par \par \uc2  ''The ringgit had an uneventful day as players are unwilling to test either the immediate resistance at 2.5500 or the immediate support of 2.5400 ringgit,'' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the trading Thursday showed little reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market. The bank borrowed three months ringgit funds at 7.00% after being absent since Jan. 24, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Money market dealers said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's borrowing Thursday was no surprise, as there were maturities on the one-month and six months funds that it previously borrowed. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had little impact in the money market. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates(KLIBOR) was at 7.12%, unchanged from Wednesday's. The three-month KLIBOR was slightly lower at 7.21%, compared with 7.22% Wednesday. The six-month KLIBOR was slightly up at 7.28% compared to 7.27% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, closed unchanged at 6.50%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0904GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2f01ewk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
