\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Down Against U.S. Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1996\par 11:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar strengthened against the Malaysian ringgit Wednesday as it broke passed the psychological 2.5600-ringgit level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market by borrowing three-month ringgit funds at 7.00%, compared to a range of between 6.85%-7.00% last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'Some players took this as a signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't increase rates further, thus they went long on the dollar,' said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Players had been cautious in the past few days believing that Bank Negara would continue to increase interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 1001 GMT, the dollar traded at 2.5634 ringgit, higher than 2.5535 ringgit late Monday and 2.5575 at the opening. During the day, it traded between 2.5528 and 2.5550 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said, was checking rates at the 2.5590 ringgit and 2.5600 ringgit level, but didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit weakened further following statements by the Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim that no new measures were needed to curb speculation. \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer with a local bank said that the ringgit was also under pressure due to cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays which favored the dollar. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) was at 7.00%, slightly lower than 7.00% on Tuesday. The three-month KLIBOR was at 7.09%, compared with 7.11% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate closed higher at 6.10% compared to Tuesday's 6.00%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1033GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1o00pzv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
