\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Down Vs Dollar; Buba Meeting Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1995\par 10:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar was stronger against the Malaysian ringgit in another day of lackluster range trading, traders said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealings, as in previous days, were confined to a tight narrow range of 2.5420 and 2.5440 ringgit, with sporadic buying coming from corporate players, said a trader. \par \par \uc2  At 0945 GMT the dollar was at 2.5435 ringgit, higher than 2.5414 ringgit late Monday. The Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.7995 ringgit, down from Monday's 1.8010 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  With no fresh news to move the market, players shifted their attention on the dollar's dealings against its major counterparts instead, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Players remained bullish on the dollar on expectations the German Bundesbank would cut its official discount rate at its regular meeting Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Should this happen, the dollar is expected to break out of the upper limit of the current range to test 2.5470 ringgit, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly but made routine checks with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in the morning, ''just to let traders know they are there,'' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, Bank Negara kept rates unchanged from Monday, accepting one-month ringgit offers at 6.50%. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were flat, with the one-month KLIBOR at 6.60%, unchanged from Monday. The three-month stood at 6.80%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate closed at 5.80%, down from Monday's 6.8%. ''The market was liquid, as there were maturities when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowed one- and three-month funds before,'' said a money market dealer.< \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0949GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbs09cpe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
