\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Slightly Down Vs Dollar; Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1995\par 11:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar was slightly up against the Malaysian ringgit and remained in tight range flat trading in a quiet market Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'There was not much movement in the market, with players showing no interest to do anything yet,' said a chief trader with a bank. \par \par \uc2  Last week's holidays in Japan and U.S. were a dampener to the market, said a trader. \par \par \uc2  There was nothing big happening, said a trader, 'even the trading against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were quiet.' \par \par \uc2  At 1017 GMT, the dollar was trading at the 2.5414 ringgit level compared to Friday's 2.5410 ringgit. Its intraday range was 2.5405 to 2.5431 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was quoted at 1.8010 ringgit up from Friday's 1.8003 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  However, traders expect the dollar ringgit trading to improve next month. 'This is when the demand for the dollar increases as traders repatriate their dollars back to their country,' said a trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara Malaysia traders said was checking rates in the morning. 'This is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's way of telling the market to limit the dollar's topside,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market by accepting one-month ringgit offers at 6.50%, keeping rates flat. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were flat, with the one-month KLIBOR at 6.60%, unchanged from Friday's, and the three-month was also unchanged at 6.80%. \par \par \uc2  But overnight rates were soft, according to a money market dealer, closing at 6.10% compared with 6.90% Friday. 'The market is flush with funds compared to last week,' said a money market dealer. 'Rates are expected to ease off further this week,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1046GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbr09d8a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
