\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Trade Gap/Amplifier-3: Awaiting Sept Figures \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 1995\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The ringgit came under selling pressure throughout the year as \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade gap widened - inspiring repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars aggressively was in early November when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the 2.5460-2.5470 ringgit level. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unsighted so far late Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended 1994 at 2.5578 ringgit, and then fell to under 2.4400 ringgit in June, before rising in the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  But the government has repeatedly stressed that since Malaysia's imports consist primarily of capital goods such as heavy machinery used in manufacturing, the prolonged period of high imports posted in the interium will eventually contribute to higher exports. \par \par \uc2  Market participants, in the absence of fresh news, have been especially cautious this week in anticipation of the September trade figures. \par \par \uc2  MMS's Tan forecasts a stronger ringgit if the September trade deficit narrows to under 700 million ringgit, and a weaker local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the trade gap widens to more than 1.3 billion ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'The market will be relatively neutral if the trade deficit is within the 900 million to 1 billion ringgit region,' said Tan. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1013GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000