\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Softer Vs Dlr Ahead Of Long Weekend \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 1995\par 04:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit is softer against the U.S. dollar early Friday as players cover their short dollar positions ahead of a three-day weekend, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to stay out of the money market since Thursday is also inspiring profit-taking on the ringgit after it rose sharply against both the U.S. and Singapore dollars earlier in the week, the chief trader of a large bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian markets close for a Hindu festival Monday. \par \par \uc2  ''It's allowing the market to consolidate, but may try to catch it by surprise at higher (dollar) levels,'' the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two-day absence, following its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in the past week, surprised dealers. ''It wants to keep the market guessing,'' a money market trader said. \par \par \uc2  So far, it hasn't tried to check the ringgit's slide, but traders believe that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to ignore the market, the dollar may try the 2.5310-2.5320 ringgit level later in the day. \par \par \uc2  At around 0202 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 2.5287 ringgit, higher than 2.5250 ringgit at the open, and 2.5280 ringgit late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates are steady, as market liquidity remains tight, traders said. Thursday the overnight rate was quoted as high as 7.00% \par \par \uc2  The one-month interbank offered rate was quoted at 6.50-6.55%, the two-month at 6.55%-6.60%, and the three-month at 6.60%-6.70%, a trader said.< \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0206GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drak08aoy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
