\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Up Vs Dlr In Quiet Listless Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 1995\par 13:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar continued to consolidate within a tight range in quiet, listless trading Tuesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0942 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5210 ringgit, down against late Monday's 2.5225 ringgit. The dollar-ringgit was trading in a tight range of 2.5189 to 2.5212 ringgit level. 'The dollar opened at 2.5210 and closed at 2.5210,' said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  'Trading was very quiet, nobody wanted to play ringgit at these levels', said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the market is unlikely to move much ahead of the Group of Seven (G-7) major industrialized countries meeting this weekend in Washington. \par \par \uc2  'No one wants to take any position at this moment,' said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders believe that the G-7 meeting would issue a statement reaffirming its commitment to a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that in the absence of fresh local factors, the dollar's performance against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would continue to dictate the ringgit's movement. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or check rates Tuesday. 'There was no reason to, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is happy with the present rates', said a trader. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, Bank Negara didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make its presence as early as Thursday as bills and other \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds mature and return to the interbank. Late Tuesday, the overnight rate was at 5.50% down from Monday's 6.25%. \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were flat, with the one-month KLIBOR at 6.05%, unchanged from Monday, and the three-month KLIBOR at 6.15%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1159GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dra307q64\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
