\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Up Vs Dlr; Further Pressure Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1995\par 12:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar continued its fall against the ringgit in slow quiet tradings Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0948 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5095 ringgit, down against late Thursday's 2.5135 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the ringgit was following the trend of the dollar yen trading. 'There was a lot of dollar selling against the yen,' said a trader with a local bank. 'It was only when the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the dollar rebounded against the yen and subsequently against the ringgit,' he said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer described Friday's trading as extremely quiet, with trading dominated by offshore buyers and sellers. \par \par \uc2  There was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or checking by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at 2.5090 ringgit and was trading in the range of 2.5060 to 2.5110 ringgit. A dealer said that the market was volatile as there was very little volume in the market. 'There is a lack of liquidity in the market,' she said. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the dollar to be pressured again next week based on its weakness against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the money market, Bank Negara didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the market was stable. Late Friday the overnight rate remained unchanged from Thursday at 6.00% \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were flat, with the one-month KLIBOR at 6.04%, down from Thursday's 6.05% , and the three-month KLIBOR at 6.14%, down from 6.15%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1012GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9t07l1x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
