\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Lower Against Dollar; No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1995\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The ringgit opened higher against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, at 2.5260 ringgit and progressing to 2.5170 ringgit, at noon traders said. \par \par \uc2  'The ringgit trading was following the dollar against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the dollar recovered when Europe started its trading day. A trader said that the Europeans were not happy with the fundamental side of the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At GMT 0905, the dollar was at 2.5205, down against late Tuesday's 2.5268 ringgit. The dollar traded in the intraday range of 2.5170 to 2.5260 ringgit, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal reserve's Federal Open Market Committee's decision to leave interest rates unchanged, had no impact on the market, traders said. 'It was already expected that it would leave rates unchanged,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or check rates Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was not as active as last week a trader said, 'Players were wounding up their dealings for the end of the month.' \par \par \uc2  In the money market, Bank Negara didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'There was no need for it to interfere as it is satisfied with the current levels,' said a money market dealer. Late Wednesday the overnight rates was 6.3% compared to 6.5% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (KLIBOR) were down, with the one-month KLIBOR at 