\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Negara  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to slow ringgit fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Madhav Reddy \par \uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Sept 21 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Bank Negara has been pumping huge funds into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since August to slow the ringgit's fall against the U.S dollar, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had cost nearly $1 billion, although they did not think it had made any net trading losses. \par \par \uc2  "At first they tried to prevent the ringgit sliding beyond 2.50 per dollar level and then, after the dollar broke through the 100-yen barrier, they have been trying to slow its fall," a dealer with a large local bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Even today, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in the market, but only checking the rates." \par \par \uc2  The daily Star newspaper said on Thursday that Bank Negara had last week spent more than $400 million to support the ringgit. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not responded to the newspaper report. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sliding against the dollar since the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began its rally against the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few weeks ago. The ringgit has declined by 3.48 percent since June 30 to about 2.5300 to a dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara confirmed its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a briefing for local media on Tuesday saying it was "aimed at smoothing out extreme fluctuations" in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not have made any losses as its trading in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have offset any notional losses on dollar/ringgit trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become extremely sensitive about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading costs since it incurred huge losses in 1992 and 1993. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9l03rei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
