\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit closes up against dollar on Negara support. \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 23 (Reuter) - The ringgit reversed its early trend to close higher against the dollar, helped by continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said profit-taking on the dollar after its strong rally recently also supported the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara came in at 2.5000 and sold the dollar down to 2.4985 this morning, dealers said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also seen constantly checking rate movements. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit closed at 2.4970/80 to the dollar, against 2.4980/90 previously. It hit an early low of 2.5005. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2.5000 on Tuesday, indicating that it wants to cap the dollar at the level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said with the dollar seen consolidating its gains, coupled with possible Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit's downside appears limited at current level. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, interbank rates were generally steady with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing one- and three-month money at 5.95 and 6.00 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at an average 6.05 percent, unchanged from Tuesday. --Syed Azman (603-2308911) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8n04oax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
