\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Falls Vs Dlr In Heavy, Active Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1995\par 10:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit is lower against the U.S. dollar Wednesday in heavy, active trade. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the dollar opened at the day's low at around 2.4500 ringgit, but took a sharp rise following the dollar's gains against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering added to the dollar's climb but traders said that for the day, it wasn't able to rise above 2.4550 ringgit because of demand for the ringgit for payment of the PETRONAS Gas Bhd. initial public offer. \par \par \uc2  -Dealings were closely tied to the yen,- the chief ringgit trader of a large local bank said. When the Bank of Japan bought dollars from 88.10 to 90.00 yen, short covering from offshore players emerged, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Many participants were caught short because sentiment towards the ringgit has turned very strong in the last two days. Since the end of last week, the dollar has dropped from its recent high of 2.4605 ringgit to current levels. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in either the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets but was heard checking dollar-ringgit rates, traders said. -He appeared happy with the current rates,- the chief trader of a leading bank said. \par \par \uc2  At around 0831 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4557 ringgit, up from 2.4522 ringgit late Tuesday, and compared with 2.4500 and 2.4555 ringgit range traded thus far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-08-95 \par \par \uc2  0835GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument