\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Lower Vs Dlr; KLIBOR Slightly Up \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1995\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit fell against the U.S. dollar Thursday in moderately active trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise against its major counterparts following a last-minute trade agreement between the U.S. and Japan helped the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise against the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  But traders said that the rise was short-lived, and reflected a kneejerk reaction as profit-taking overwhelmed the dollar's modest gains. \par \par \uc2  Around 0934 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4405 ringgit, higher than 2.4386 ringgit around the same time Wednesday, and 2.4425 ringgit early Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its morning tender and borrowed one-month money at the same rates at 5.74%-5.75%. \par \par \uc2  At the late-morning fixing, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) was quoted unchanged at 5.85%. The one-month rate was fixed at 5.77%, slightly higher than 5.75% Wednesday, and the one-year KLIBOR was at 6.09%, also higher than 6.05% before. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0944GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6t04ybq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
