\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Flat Vs Dlr; KLIBOR Softer \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1995\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit kept to a tight trading range Tuesday, but trading was moderately active, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Following major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings, the dollar traded within a 10 point range through the day as participants awaited leads from U.S.-Japan trade talks and next week's Federal Reserve Open Market committee meeting. \par \par \uc2  -We don't see the dollar trading out of the current 2.4300-2.4400 ringgit range in the short term,- a trader with a large local bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said that sentiment for the ringgit remains very bullish although cross-trade with the Singapore dollar has subsided in the last few days. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar traded well above 1.7600 ringgit until early this month when interest rate differentials between Singapore and Malaysia fuelled buying of the ringgit. The S$ touched a recent low of 1.7425 ringgit but isn't expected to trade outside of 1.7300-1.7500 ringgit in the next month , a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Around 1006 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 2.4370 ringgit, lower than 2.4378 ringgit around the same time Monday, and unchanged from 2.4370 ringgit at the open Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, rates slipped further, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its morning tender and borrowed one-month money at the same rates at 5.74%-5.75%. \par \par \uc2  At the late-morning fixing, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) was quoted at 5.85%, down from 5.87% Monday. The one-month 