\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Little Moved Vs Dlr; KLIBOR Softer \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1995\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit kept to a tight trading range Monday, ending little changed from late Friday's levels against the U.S. dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealings were quiet and followed the lackluster trend in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings elsewhere, a trader with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Instead, trade focused on continued profit-taking of the ringgit against the Singapore dollar. Cross trade pushed the ringgit to recent year highs in the last week. \par \par \uc2  Around 0840 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 2.4378 ringgit, flat from 2.4377 ringgit late Friday, and 2.4376 ringgit at the open Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that despite the lack of movement in the market, sentiment continues to be bullish on the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, rates trended softer after last week's short squeeze sent short-end rates higher. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its morning tender and borrowed one-month money at the same rates at 5.74%-5.75%. \par \par \uc2  At the late-morning fixing, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) was quoted at 5.87%, down from 5.90% Friday. The one-month rate was fixed at 5.76%, also lower than 5.80% previously, while the one-year KLIBOR was unchanged at 6.20%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0845GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6q04rsx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoa