\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Steady Vs Dlr; Sentiment Cautious \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1995\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit was flat against the U.S. dollar Wednesday in fairly active trading with sentiment was on the cautious side ahead of the Group of Seven (G-7) meeting Thursday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said some offshore players were selling the ringgit against the dollar but commercial demand for the ringgit from exporters helped steadied the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the close, the dollar was quoted at 2.4390 ringgit, unchanged from Tuesday's close. Trading was still ranged bound. \par \par \uc2  'Market players weren't sure what will emerge from the G-7 meeting, particularly on decisions which could affect the dollar,' the chief dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, longer-term interbank rates were still under pressure to ease. Short-term rates were holding because of Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowed one-month deposits via the open tender system at between 5.74% and 5.75%. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) were unchanged at 5.75% but the three-month rate edged lower to 5.83% from 5.85% Tuesday. The 12-month rate was fixed at 6.16% from 6.20% previously. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0913GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6e04f33\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
