\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian Ringgit Falls Sharply Vs Dlr; Volatile Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1995\par 11:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-DJ)--The Malaysian ringgit came under selling pressure Friday to end sharply lower against the U.S. dollar in thin trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said the ringgit was tracking the dollar which has been rising against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. \par \par \uc2  At the close, the dollar was higher at 2.4950 ringgit, up 265 points from 2.4685 ringgit Thursday. It hit an intra-day high of 2.5010 ringgit in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Trading was thin but very volatile, fluctuating within a wide band of around 300 points, the chief dealer of a large Malaysian bank said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the ringgit's sharp drop, Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. 'But if the ringgit continues to drop, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to come in,' he added. \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer said trading was thin largely because most players weren't eager to take positions ahead of the long weekend. The market is closed on Monday for a religious holiday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-05-95 \par \par \uc2  0929GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr5c03h1j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
