\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit rise vs dlr may run out of steam - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Reme Ahmad \par \uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, April 17 (Reuter) - The ringgit, trading around nine-year highs against the dollar, could run out of steam at around 2.45 ringgit as Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wary of losing the country's export competitiveness, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Although global dollar weakness will support further strengthening of the ringgit in the near term, there is increasing expectation that Bank Negara's tolerance level may be breached soon, they said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit has risen by some 3.3 percent against the dollar this year and by 2.4 percent in the last two weeks alone. \par \par \uc2  "Negara is reluctant to see the ringgit appreciate too rapidly as it hurts exporters," said Paul Schymyck, regional economist at Smith Barney Shearson HG Asia. \par \par \uc2  In 1994, Malaysia exported 21 percent of its products to the U.S., its number one export market. The exports, mainly electrical and electronic goods, were worth some 32.52 billion ringgit ($13.19 billion), Bank Negara estimated. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit rose to a nine-year high of 2.4580 ringgit to the dollar in early Kuala Lumpur trade on Monday, the first time the 2.4600 level has been broken since January 1986. \par \par \uc2  It retreated later on profit taking, to end at 2.4650/60 ringgit, hardly changed from 2.4645/55 ringgit on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be swift if it feels the ringgit's spiral has been overdone, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly warned against a rapid rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara governor Ahmad Mohamad Don said recently "If (the ringgit) appreciates too much in a very short period of time, we have to come in to stabilise the market." \par \par \uc2  He said at the presentation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1994 annual report on March 29 that Bank Negara could tolerate a higher \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it reflects \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past when the ringgit threatened to jump by between 300-500 points in a day, said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Bank Negara had tolerated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's jump in recent weeks to try reduce the impact of the mighty yen on the economy. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit has fallen by 12.7 percent against the yen this year, affecting the ringgit's rate in Malaysia's basket of trade \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "On a trade-weighted basis, there's not been much change for the ringgit," said Marco Wong, director at Yamaichi Capital Management. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, 100 yen was worth 3.0049/65 ringgit. The ringgit was also at 1.7804/26 marks. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is expected to end the year at around 2.45-2.50 to the dollar, suported by expectations of higher interest rates in Malaysia, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  --Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-2308911) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4h08ixc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
