\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit jump vs dollar has Negara's nod - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Reme Ahmad \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, April 14 (Reuter) - The ringgit's sharp spiral against the dollar has the quiet blessing of Malaysia's Bank Negara as it tries to reduce the impact of the mighty yen on the economy, economists and dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is set to test nine-year highs versus the dollar soon, but Bank Negara, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop or even try to slow the surge recently, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Our impression is that Bank Negara is not concerned about the rate of the dollar-ringgit," said Andy Tan, economist at MMS International, a Standard & Poor's company. \par \par \uc2  "When the ringgit appreciates against the dollar, the ringgit will depreciate more slowly against the yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  With a huge inflow of capital goods from Japan, Bank Negara is using the dollar-ringgit weakness to hedge against the rise of the yen-ringgit, economists said. \par \par \uc2  Japan, Malaysia's biggest trading partner, accounted for 26.7 percent its total imports of 156 billion ringgit ($63 billion) in 1994. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's trade deficit with Japan grew to around 23 billion ringgit ($9 billion) last year, against 17 billion ($7 billion) in the previous year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the country's deficit, forecast at 13.8 billion ringgit ($5.5 billion) in the current year, could balloon further if the yen's rise against the ringgit is not checked. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit has risen by 3.3 percent against the dollar this year, but has fallen by some 12.7 percent versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  At mid-mmorning on Friday, the ringgit was at 2.4670/80 ringgit-to-the-dollar against 2.5490/00 on Jan 3. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was also at 2.9169/07 per 100 yen, against 2.5442/64 at the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inaction may also be due to the fact that it wants the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate before hiking interest rates later to cool an overheating economy. \par \par \uc2  "It will be the perfect textbook situation where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first lets the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise and then raise interest rates," said one economist. "There won't be a flow of speculative funds and Negara will be perceived as a competent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara imposed a series of capital controls beginning in January of 1994 after a sudden gush of hot money poured into the banking system. The bank said it feared the flood of funds was threatening its control over the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The controls have largely been lifted. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's key three-month interbank rate has risen sharply this year after two years of decline. It was at 6.08 percent on Friday against 5.44 percent at the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4e08qfw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
