\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit ends unchanged vs dollar in choppy trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, March 28 (Reuter) - The ringgit closed unchanged against the dollar after a choppy trading session dominated by offshore selling of ringgit and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Negara was checking rates throughout the day and did hit the market near the close," said one dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at 2.5390, apparently wanting to cap the dollar at 2.54. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was brief and much smaller than its earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit ended at 2.5385/95 to the dollar, unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly over the two previous sessions to ward off ringgit-selling from offshore banks and to drive up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of its annual report, due to be released on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said concern about Malaysia's current account deficit has led to the foreign selling of the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara has forecast a deficit of 12 billion ringgit for 1994, but there has been speculation that the deficit could reach 17 billion. \par \par \uc2  --Syed Azman (603-2308911) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr3s096ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
