\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit closes higher vs dollar on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 113 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Jan 13 (Reuter) - The ringgit reversed its early trend to close higher against the dollar after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The ringgit was heading lower before Bank Negara came in at around the 2.56 level. Players then gradually bought back the ringgit," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit ended at 2.5590/00 to the dollar, against 2.5611/21 on Thursday, after trading at an early low of 2.5640. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had came under pressure from foreign fund selling on rumours of devaluation in some of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . --Syed Azman (603-2308911) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr1d0896m\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (malaysia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl